== body of 257: size and head
21458
Issue 03 of 22 of the plan #254. Key: `access`. Level 0. Size L.

## Outcome

4 of the 30 auth routes answer, and the others answer 404. The service stores no GitHub user token, and one UPDATE clears the tokens that production holds today. Each private request pays less for the access check: no schema check, and fewer D1 round trips.

## Why

**Routes.** Better Auth serves 30 routes, and the app uses 4 (TRUST-01). The service is safer when a route that nobody calls does not answer.

**Tokens.** The service stores the GitHub user token of each sign-in, and it has no use for that token (AUTH-16). A stored value with no use is a risk with no gain.

**Session values.** The session handling is stricter than today after rows 3 and 5 of the list (AUTH-09, AUTH-14).

**Cost.** Better Auth checks the complete database schema on each request (LOAD-01, AUTH-01, API-01, and 5 more findings of high severity). In the model of the audit, the run list moves from 1,190 to 817 ms with the first-page fixes. The access check makes more D1 round trips than it needs (measured on a local D1, D-LOAD-03). The private brief has the two numbers.

**Order of the checks.** Some request paths do other work before they check the credential (AUTH-07, TRUST-10, TRUST-09). 3 rows change an answer code in an edge case.

Labels of the facts: "measured" is a number that the audit measured, "counted from code" is a fact that was read in the code of 2026-10-07, "from the record" is a statement of the audit that this plan did not check again, and "assumption" is a statement that nobody checked. A fact with a finding identifier and no label is from the record. Each defect that this issue names is in the code of the branch `main` of 2026-10-07. Two names of the audit: the rule "no backward compatibility" is the standing rule of the maintainer that no backward compatibility is necessary while Ariakit is the only consumer, and the helper that counts D1 writes is `apps/web/src/api/test-d1-costs.ts`.

Findings of the audit in this issue: 32. A row of an accepted fix list (15): AUTH-06, AUTH-07, AUTH-09, AUTH-12, AUTH-13, AUTH-14, AUTH-15, AUTH-17, LOAD-01, TRUST-01, TRUST-02, TRUST-05, TRUST-09, TRUST-10, TRUST-11. Covered by a settled answer (17): AUTH-01, AUTH-02, AUTH-03, AUTH-04, AUTH-05, AUTH-16, API-01, API-05, API-06, REVIEW-01, REVIEW-15, LIVE-01, LOAD-09, LOAD-14, INFRA-01, D1-01, D1-02.

## Decisions

Each block has the settled answer in full, as the maintainer selected it. The answer is the
